ted, _server=None), close() from a foreign thread keeps library semantics, defusal is identity-keyed not name-keyed (impostor threads with the same name still join), guard caches per base and passes non-class doubles through, and the loader-routes-live-class wiring is pinned. Full suite with the sentinel installed: 1171 passed / 0 failed in 217s (matches the 218s pre-fix baseline; an intermediate 577s run was ambient load, reproduced clean on rerun); the only sentinel hit across two full runs is the bug-pin test itself. Nothing pushed; user's unrelated uncommitted files untouched.

