2026-09-20 | src/the_oracle/pipeline.py + src/the_oracle/utils/audio.py + tests/test_stem_cache_write_path.py (new) + tests/test_vulkan_render.py | Stem-cache write-path audit (end-to-end): the engine-output gate is verified as the only spoken-stem writer, and the cache's trust-on-existence read behavior is closed. Findings: (1) the batched Vulkan path's cache-hit branch trusted stem_path.exists() alone — never even loadability — so any garbage/degenerate byte content on disk was served as a hit; (2) the all-cached fast path checked only exists() in its skip-decision; (3) pause-only tasks reached the BATCHED path carrying text="" and shipped empty text to audio.cpp, whose silent decode now fails the hardening gate and would take the whole batch down (a latent interaction introduced BY the hardening, found by this audit); (4) the sequential spoken path ran only the loadability check, so a pre-hardening degenerate entry (valid WAV, silent/DC content) was served forever. Fixes: stem_is_speech_like (utils/audio.py) — the write gate's taxonomy as a read predicate, allow_silence exempting pause-only stems; _load_servable_stem (pipeline.py) — loads, re-classifies, deletes unservable entries (degenerate -> cache miss + re-synthesis), wired into all three read routes (sequential spoken, batched hits, all-cached fast path); the batched path now banks pause-only stems itself at _PAUSE_STEM_FALLBACK_SAMPLE_RATE (24000, Chatterbox's canonical rate, assemble_dialogue's own fallback — mismatches still fail loudly at assembly) and completes their results off the engine group; _load_cached_stem demoted to the wrapper's inner loader. Writer manifest test: AST scan of every stem/preview-shaped save_wav/atomic_write call — all 5 land in pipeline.py + real_engine_smoke.py (gated owners), with a >=4 blindness guard. One test-fixture correction: test_vulkan_render_mixed_cache_progress_never_rewinds seeded cache hits with np.zeros — loadable degenerate content the read gate now (correctly) refuses; fixture swapped to a ramp, preserving the test's actual subject (progress monotonicity). Honest scope: the read gate retroactively purges pre-hardening entries whose degeneracy the taxonomy recognizes (silence/DC/NaN/empty) on first read; entries degenerate in unrecognized ways (e.g. distorted-but-nonzero audio) are still servable — content alone cannot distinguish them. 18 new tests: predicate taxonomy, sequential stale-hit deletion + pause-hit silence + healthy hit, batched spoken-hit revalidation + pause banked-off-engine (a test bug caught the first draft falling through to pending.append and shipping empty text anyway — restructured so pause tasks complete their result in the loop), healthy batch hit, write-gate contract round trip, writer manifest, deletion round trip. Full suite 1189 passed / 0 failed (1171 + 18). Nothing pushed; user's unrelated uncommitted files untouched.

2026-09-21 | src/the_oracle/utils/audio.py, src/the_oracle/tts_engines/chatterbox_engine.py,
src/the_oracle/tts_engines/vulkan_backend.py | tests/test_synthesis_retry.py (12)
One-shot fresh-seed resynthesis retry: sanitizer rejections self-heal once.
The engine output gate (sanitize_engine_audio) now raises DegenerateEngineOutput
(a ValueError subclass) so the engines can distinguish hiccup rejections from
unrelated ValueErrors. ChatterboxEngine.synthesize splits into a seed-parameterized
_generate_once + a one-shot retry wrapper; AudioCppVulkanEngine does the same for
the single subprocess path (sentinel _USE_CONFIGURED_SEED threads an explicit
retry seed into the --seed flag) and for the batch path (gate rejections are
collected per request, successful outputs kept, only rejected requests re-run in
a fresh subprocess at seed+1, second rejection raises the lowest original index).
Critical mechanic: both engines re-apply their seed on EVERY call (torch
manual_seed / --seed flag), so a naive retry would deterministically reproduce
the same degenerate output — the retry always carries seed+1 when configured,
or stays unseeded (fresh randomness). Batch retry never re-fires
on_request_complete (progress maps batch-local indexes to tasks; re-firing
would double-count). Second rejection propagates so the stem is never cached.
Full suite: 1201 passed / 0 failed (1189 + 12).

2026-09-21 | scripts/release.py | tests/test_release.py (+8), STATE.md
Release --check verifies the CHANGELOG: the current version must have exactly
one '## [<version>] — <YYYY-MM-DD>' section, dated the release day. New
changelog_problems() runs alongside the pyproject/banner probes; --check grew
an injectable `today` (keyword-only) so tests pin the mechanics on any date.
The regex pins the canonical heading (em dash, zero-padded date); near-misses
(hyphen, bolded, no brackets, 1-digit fields) report as "missing" so
hand-written variants cannot satisfy the invariant, and date.fromisoformat
rejects impossible calendar days (2026-13-45). Design consequence, deliberate:
undated --check passes only ON the release day — between releases it fails
with the exact heading to add, making the gate a release-day checklist item
(bump version → changelog heading dated today → --sync-banners → commit →
build). test_check_passes_on_this_repo became
test_check_passes_on_this_repo_on_its_own_release_day: it evaluates the real
repo's check at the date stamped on its current section, so the invariant is
pinned on real content without being hostage to the calendar. Full suite:
1209 passed / 0 failed (1201 + 8).

